    "BrochureContent": [
      {
        "ContentType": "Description",
        "SortOrder": 0,
        "Content": "\nNo. 15 Woodstock is a well-appointed four-bedroom semi-detached home offering spacious and exceptionally versatile accommodation over three levels. Enjoying an efficient B Energy Rating, an extended open-plan kitchen / dining space, a generously configured converted attic room and a substantial log cabin in the rear garden, this impressive property has been thoughtfully configured and is sure to appeal to a wide variety of buyers.\n \nUpon entering, a welcoming hallway provides access to a guest WC and convenient utility room. To the front, the living room is a bright and inviting reception room overlooking the driveway through a large box bay window. A wood-burning stove creates a warm focal point. To the rear of the home lies an impressive extended kitchen / dining room designed for both everyday living and entertaining. The kitchen is fitted with extensive cabinetry, marble worktops and a comprehensive selection of integrated appliances, while a central breakfast bar provides more space for dining. Double doors lead directly to the rear garden, while an adjoining light-filled playroom provides a versatile additional space. Upstairs, the principal bedroom is a generous double room positioned to the front, complete with extensive fitted wardrobes, a box bay window and an en-suite shower room. Two further bedrooms overlook the rear garden, while a fourth bedroom to the front is currently arranged as a study, offering flexibility for those working from home. A well-appointed family bathroom completes the first-floor accommodation.\n\nThe attic level is a superb addition to the overall accommodation. Generously proportioned and illuminated by four Velux windows, this versatile room benefits from fitted wardrobes, extensive eaves storage and an adjoining shower room. It offers excellent flexibility for a variety of uses, whether as a home office, gym or additional guest space.\nOutside, the rear garden has been thoughtfully designed with ease of maintenance and family enjoyment in mind. An Indian sandstone patio provides an ideal setting for al fresco dining, while the artificial lawn offers a practical year-round play area. The garden is enclosed by timber fencing and further enhanced by outdoor lighting and an impressive built-in play structure.\n\nA particular highlight is the detached log cabin, extending to approximately 15 sq.m. This substantial and versatile space offers excellent potential as a home office, gym or storage space, depending on one's needs. \n\nWoodstock is a popular residential development within easy reach of Kilcoole village and its range of local shops, schools, services and sporting amenities. Kilcoole enjoys the best of coast and countryside, with scenic walks, Kilcoole Beach and the surrounding North Wicklow landscape all close at hand. The village is served by local bus routes and commuter rail services, while the N11 is accessible via Greystones/Delgany.\nViewing is highly recommended to fully appreciate all that this impressive home has to offer."
      },
      {
        "ContentType": "Accommodation",
        "SortOrder": 1,
        "Content": "\nEntrance Hall - \nNew composite door, wired for alarm, tiled floor, access to downstairs WC and utility room.\n\nLiving Room - 3.59m x 6.08m\nReception room to front, picture window overlooking front driveway. Mantelpiece with wood-fired stove. TV point.\n\nKitchen/Dining - 5.54m x 6m\nExtended open plan kitchen/dining space, marble countertops. Extensive eye and floor level units with tiled splashback, integrated Neff oven, grill, microwave & 5 ring gas hob with overhead Rangemaster fan, Integrated dishwasher. Provision for fridge/freezer. Central countertops with breakfast bar and ample power outlets, leading to bright open space to rear filled with light from floor to ceiling glass windows and Velux roof window. TV point. Double doors lead to rear garden.\n\nUtility Room - \nPositioned off the kitchen, built-in storage units and provision for washing machine / dryer.\n\nDownstairs WC - \nWC, wash-hand basin\n\nUpstairs Landing - \nAccess to hot press and attic room.\n\nBedroom 1 - 2.6m x 4.4m\nSpacious double room to front with extensive built in wardrobes. Box bay window overlooking driveway. Leads to;\n\nEn-Suite - \nFloor to ceiling tiling, WC, wash had basin, chrome heated towel rail, step in shower with sliding screen door. Extractor fan.\n\nBedroom 2 - 2.74m x 3.46m\nSpacious double room overlooking garden. TV point.\n\nBedroom 3 - 2.7m x 2.55m\nSingle room to rear\n\nBedroom 4/Study - 2.2m x 3.22m\nSingle room to front currently in used as a study.\n\nFamily Bathroom - \nFloor to ceiling tiling, WC, wash hand basin, bath with showerhead attachment.\n\nAttic Room - 4.9m x 4.2m\nWell configured attic room with 4 Velux windows and built-in wardrobes. Eaves storage and TV point. Leads to;\n\nShower - \nWC, wash hand basin, tiled wall and floor, shower with sliding screen door. Chrome heated towel rail and Velux window.\n\nOutside - \nRear garden is laid in Indian sandstone patio with low maintenance Astro turf lawn. Bordered by timber fencing with outdoor lighting and impressive built in playground structure and garden room measuring 15 sqm approx. To the front of the home is a driveway providing off-street parking.\n\n"
      },
      {
        "ContentType": "Features",
        "SortOrder": 3,
        "Content": "<ul><li>Special Features:</li><li>Rear garden access is through a locked gate with an awning running the full length of the property providing secure rear garden access and additional storage for bicycles etc</li><li>Well-appointed four-bedroom semi-detached home</li><li>Light-filled interior</li><li>Remote Hive heating system</li><li>Comprehensive CCTV system with 7 cameras accessible through mobile app</li><li>Alarm system with fire detection system incorporated, accessible through your mobile for personal monitoring </li><li>Off-street parking</li><li>Attic conversion</li><li>Versatile outdoor log cabin</ul>"
      },
